    <profile id="4e4d-4996-5a6f-afbc" name="Hallucinogen Grenades" hidden="false" typeId="7279-038a-b87a-ed0c" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a08a-36f8-2fd3-b843">In the turn the Harlequins charged into combat, when working out if one side outnumbers the other after an assault, the ratio of models is shifted one "grade" in favor of the Harlequins.
These grenades do not work against Daemons, Wraithlords, Wraithguard, Dark Eldar Talos and Warp Beasts, Thousand Sons, Necrons, or Vehicles. Against Tyranids the Tyranid unit ignores the grenade on a D6 roll of 1.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile id="d753-c022-6f20-41a9" name="Tanglefoot Grenades" hidden="false" typeId="7279-038a-b87a-ed0c" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a08a-36f8-2fd3-b843">In the turn the Harlequines charge into combat, if the unit attacked fails it morale check its fall back move is D6 less than normal. If the Harlequins break then their enemy may only consolidate. In the event of a drawn combat, then the unit fighting the Harlequins may not move any unengaged models into combat.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
